# Example program

# < - this is a comment
# lines starting with that are not evaluated
# it must be the first character

# The VM impliments New to define a variable,
# Mod to modify an existing variable, Call to
# call a function, Func to define a function,
# and End to end a function. 
# New and Mod can perform basic argerithmatic
# operations based on a left and right source
# with one operator (eg. 3 + 4 but not 3 + 4 + 5).
# The standard library defines common functions
# like Print, GetInput, and so on. It should be
# copy-pasted to the start of the source code
# file.
# Syntax is known to use ( ) for VM defined
# operations.
# Two types exist - numb for numbers and
# string for strings. 
# Examples
# New var ( string hi ) # allocate var
# var as a string with hi
# Mod var ( string hello ) # modify var
# var to now hold string with hello
# Mod var ( numb 12 ) # and so on
# If exists under syntax If ( condition )
# It behaves like a function that is
# executed if the condition is true.

# Here is a simple program

New a ( numb 12 )
New b ( numb a + 20 )
New msg ( string Hello )
New ARG1 ( string msg )
Call Print
New x ( numb 6 )
If ( x > 5 )
Mod msg ( string greater )
Call Print
End
Func ( func )
Mod msg ( string func )
Call Print
End
Call func
